{
  "body_human_readable": "### \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy\" Soars Past $100 Million Worldwide\n\nThe 2005 film adaptation of Douglas Adams' beloved science fiction novel, \"The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy,\" grossed over $100 million at the worldwide box office. The movie was produced with a budget of approximately $45 to $50 million.\n\nAccording to financial data from Box Office Mojo, the film's worldwide box office total reached $102,746,214. The-Numbers.com reports a production budget of $45 million for the movie. Another source corroborates a worldwide gross of $104,478,416 and lists the budget in the range of $45\u201350 million.\n\nThe film's domestic performance in the United States accounted for $51,019,112, with the international box office contributing $51,727,102. The movie opened in first place in North America, earning $21,103,203 in its debut weekend. In the United Kingdom, it premiered a day earlier and garnered \u00a34,200,000 in its first week.",
